Package: dosopt
Type: Package
Title: Utility Score Framework for Dose Optimization Studies
Version: 0.1.0
Date: 2026-02-18
Authors@R: c(
    person("Xuemin", "Gu", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "xuemin.gu@bicycletx.com"),
    person("Cong", "Xu", role = "aut"),
    person("Lei", "Xu", role = "aut"),
    person("Ying", "Yuan", role = "aut"))
Description: Implements a frequentist framework for one-stage randomized dose
    optimization studies under the FDA Project Optimus initiative. The package
    provides: (1) a margin-based utility score approach integrating binary
    efficacy and safety endpoints; (2) closed-form and exact sample size
    formulas to achieve prespecified Probabilities of Correct Selection (PCS);
    (3) analytical expressions for selection-induced bias in response rate
    estimation; (4) Type I error inflation calculations for binary and
    time-to-event confirmatory endpoints; and (5) Monte Carlo simulation
    validation. The framework generalizes the one-stage Randomized Optimal
    Selection (ROSE) design as a special case. An interactive Shiny application
    is included for design exploration and simulation.
